 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t one objectively “best” company for every Atlanta home, but **The Air Company** looks like a reasonable first call: it serves Atlanta, advertises AC replacement, and says it has NATE-certified technicians and an unrestricted Georgia license. Those are company-reported credentials, so verify them before hiring.\n\nFor a major purchase, get **at least three written quotes**—for example, also contact **Reliable Heating & Air** (a long-established Atlanta-area provider) and **Estes Services**. Compare more than the equipment price: ask whether the quote includes a proper load calculation, permits, ductwork changes if needed, labor and parts warranties, and removal of the old unit. Verify the contractor’s Georgia conditioned-air license and insurance, and don’t choose based on a star rating alone.",
